# VTID-03910/03911 — commands run during this change

## Investigation: live-browser-equivalent verification harness

Since this session has no live authenticated Command Hub browser session,
built a local static harness (`/tmp/.../verify-operator-ui/harness.html`)
that loads the real `services/gateway/src/frontend/command-hub/styles.css`
and mirrors the exact DOM class structure `renderOperatorOverlay()`/
`renderOperatorChat()` produce, then drove it with Playwright
(chromium at /opt/pw-browsers/chromium-1194, NODE_PATH pointed at the
global playwright install since this repo has no local playwright dep).

This caught the real VTID-03911 root cause directly: `page.locator(...)
.evaluate(el => getComputedStyle(el))` on the mic button right after a
click showed `border: rgb(148, 163, 184)` (the neutral :hover color) even
though `el.className` correctly included `chat-mic-btn--active` — proving
a CSS specificity bug, not a JS logic bug.

